# Build output
bin/
obj/
dist/

# Runtime state: the game writes this beside itself on exit.
big2.ini

# Deny-by-default for documentation.
#
# Everything in this project except the README is internal -- working notes, the
# differences record, session logs. Listing them individually means the next new
# note is tracked by accident, and the ignore file then has to name the very
# documents that must not be named anywhere public. Excluding the whole class
# and re-admitting one file is the only arrangement that stays correct as
# documents are added.
#
# Here it is a second line of defence rather than the first: this repository's
# boundary sits BELOW the internal material, which lives one directory up and so
# cannot be committed from inside the working tree at all.
*.md
!README.md

# Push-guard terms. Untracked on purpose: publishing them defeats the guard.
.githooks/forbidden-terms
